Coral reefs exhibit a wide range of colors due to the symbiotic relationship between corals and algae (zooxanthellae). Common colors include vibrant reds, yellows, oranges, greens, purples, and pinks. The coloration can vary depending on the species of coral and environmental factors like light exposure and water temperature.

